; Chart of accounts — every account is opened exactly once, here, grouped by kind.
; Naming: Assets:US:<Institution>:<Name><last4> | Liabilities:US:<Institution>:Card<last4>
;         Income:US:<Source> | Expenses:<Category>[:Subcategory]

; Every account's open directive carries `owner:` metadata — the household
; lens. Owners are the household's own lowercase names (match facts/people/
; file names) plus "joint" for shared accounts; the vocabulary comes from the
; household, not this template. It powers `query.py networth --by-owner` and
; `balances`, the owners section of reports/summary.json, and the owner
; labels on the home page's money map — and the cross-check gate proves the
; per-owner slices re-add to liquid net worth to the cent. Untagged accounts
; roll up as "unassigned"; when unsure, use "joint".

; --- Bank & cards (add as institutions are onboarded), e.g.
; 2025-01-01 open Assets:US:<Bank>:Checking1234        USD
;   owner: "alex"
; 2025-01-01 open Assets:US:<Bank>:Savings9876         USD  ; shared emergency fund
;   owner: "joint"
; 2025-01-01 open Liabilities:US:<Bank>:Card5678       USD
;   owner: "jordan"

; --- Investments (add as institutions are onboarded) ---

; --- Clearing & equity ---
2000-01-01 open Equity:Opening-Balances
2000-01-01 open Assets:US:Transfers            USD  ; own-account transfer clearing (should net to ~0)

; --- Income ---
2000-01-01 open Income:US:Interest              USD
2000-01-01 open Income:US:Other                 USD  ; unmatched credits — reclassify via rules.toml

; --- Expenses — the starter set the default rules.toml can produce. Grow it. ---
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Uncategorized         USD  ; the review queue — should trend to zero
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Cash                  USD  ; ATM / cash withdrawals
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Food:Dining           USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Food:Groceries        USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Shopping              USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Travel                USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Transport             USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Health                USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Entertainment         USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Personal              USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Gifts                 USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Home                  USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Utilities             USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Education             USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Services              USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Fees                  USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Insurance             USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Housing               USD
2000-01-01 open Expenses:Taxes                 USD

; Commodities you hold get declared once. Tag market-traded ones with a
; price source and scripts/update_prices.sh keeps them current. The
; asset_allocation_* metadata (percentages, must sum to 100) feeds fava's
; Investor -> Asset Allocation Classes page:
;   2020-01-01 commodity VTSAX
;     name: "Vanguard Total Stock Market Index Admiral"
;     price: "USD:yahoo/VTSAX"
;     asset_allocation_equity_us: 100
